        "value": "Shizoku population: 250 persons — followed by a small editorial （ママ）'sic' marker, printed as （マヽ）, set beside the figure at the right of the column. The marker is there because the male/female split directly below sums to 251 (133 + 118), not 250: the 1928 editors are recording that 二百五十 stands as printed in the original. This is the only arithmetic failure on the page, and the only （ママ）on it. The box is widened to enclose the marker with the figure it qualifies."
